      "text": "Let the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) be given as \\(\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nAccording to the problem statement, we have the following system of equations, derived from the given conditions:\n\n1. \\(\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix} \\implies \\begin{cases} 3a = 6, \\\\ 3c = 21 \\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nFrom the second equation of the system, we get:\n\n\\[\n3c = 21 \\implies c = 7\n\\]\n\nFrom the first equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n3a = 6 \\implies a = 2\n\\]\n\n2. \\(\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -a + 5b \\\\ -c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix} \\implies \\begin{cases} -a + 5b = 3 \\\\ -c + 5d = -17 \\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values \\(a = 2\\) and \\(c = 7\\), we obtain:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases} -2 + 5b = 3, \\\\ -7 + 5d = -17 \\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSolving the first equation for \\(b\\):\n\\[\n-2 + 5b = 3 \\implies 5b = 5 \\implies b = 1\n\\]\n\nSolving the second equation for \\(d\\):\n\\[\n-7 + 5d = -17 \\implies 5d = -10 \\implies d = -2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe code implementation is as follows:\n\nLet's quickly check and display the result for correctness.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define variables\na, b, c, d = sp.symbols('a b c d')\n\n# Define the matrix M\nM = sp.Matrix([[a, b], [c, d]])\n\n# Define the first condition\ncond1 = M * sp.Matrix([3, 0]) == sp.Matrix([6, 21])\n\n# Solve the first condition\nsolutions = sp.solve(cond1, (a, b, c, d))\n\n# Substitute these into the second condition\nM = M.subs(solutions)\n\nprint(M)\n````",
